From 92ac78797b6417d293bf3efcd715cdb5e214705f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "vivy (opencode agent)" <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:28:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] oplus-fwk: back the AOSP-mappable OplusEdrUtils members

OplusEdrUtils was entirely stubbed, so every EDR call from the stock camera
returned false or null. Fill only the members that have a 1:1 primitive in
the framework we actually build against, and leave the rest exactly as they
were. The restraint is the point: probe.md 6 and the postboot matrix prove
only EIGHT AGGREGATE dex references from OplusCamera to this class, and no
permitted artifact maps those references to individual methods. Per-method
reachability is therefore unresolved, and filling a member on the strength of
a class-level reference count would be guessing at an ABI.

Backed here, each against frameworks_base 043337ae:

  setEdrSdrRatio         -> SurfaceControl.Transaction.setDesiredHdrHeadroom
                            (SurfaceControl.java:4955)
  getSurfaceControl      -> View.getViewRootImpl (View.java:21511) then
                            ViewRootImpl.getSurfaceControl (ViewRootImpl.java:12264)
  getBlastSurfaceControl -> SurfaceView.getRenderingSurfaceControl
                            (SurfaceView.java:1487), which returns the same
                            mBlastSurfaceControl the OOS name refers to

The two accessors are not padding: setEdrSdrRatio needs a SurfaceControl, and
without them the caller can only ever hand it null, which would make the
backed member unreachable in practice.

Guarding is what keeps this from being a regression. setDesiredHdrHeadroom
calls checkPreconditions(sc) and then throws IllegalArgumentException unless
the ratio is finite and either 0 or >= 1.0f, so an unguarded bridge would
convert a silent stub into a camera-visible crash - strictly worse than the
stub it replaced. Out-of-domain ratios are rejected with the API's existing
"not applied" false rather than clamped, since clamping would quietly change
what the caller asked for. Every bridge is additionally wrapped, so no
throwable escapes into the app.

Deliberately NOT done:

  - No gpu_tonemapper bridge. probe.md 4 surveyed it at ad047687 and found a
    generic GL 3D-LUT engine with no HDR headroom or ratio input, no stock
    HLG/PQ transfer math, and no caller of its factory anywhere in the open
    display trees. It cannot supply headroom, so wiring to it would be
    invention.
  - No gainmap fill. AOSP has no gainmap primitive on SurfaceControl
    .Transaction: setGainmap matches 0 lines in SurfaceControl.java while
    setDesiredHdrHeadroom matches in the same file, so the absence is a
    controlled result and not a failed search. setEdrGainmapInfo stays a stub.
  - No device commit. The sdrHdrRatioMap this feature ultimately depends on
    lands in the brightness topic's single authoritative displayconfig.xml
    commit; this topic cuts no device tree change.

Recorded assumption EDR-1: non-throwing stubs plus these AOSP-backed members
are sufficient for the stock camera to launch and preview. Post-flash check is
probe.md 8.2 - resolve and launch com.oplus.camera, then grep the buffer for
OplusEdrUtils, setDesiredHdrHeadroom, IllegalArgument, FATAL EXCEPTION and
AndroidRuntime, requiring no row. If that grep names a specific member, that
member is the wave-4 input; an unresolved activity or an empty buffer is not a
pass.

Ultraworked with [Sisyphus](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent)

Icp-Layer: restub
Icp-Class: required-camera-support
Icp-Restubs: OplusEdrUtils AOSP-primitive-backed members (setEdrSdrRatio, getSurfaceControl, getBlastSurfaceControl) - OplusCamera launch/preview path
Icp-Undoes: android_hardware_oplus:oplus-fwk/src/com/oplus/view/OplusEdrUtils.java - the fully stubbed EDR surface that returned false/null for every call
Upstream-Half: sibling orgs adopt only the same AOSP-backed compatibility members their own OplusCamera requires, and keep the rest stubbed until per-method reachability is proven
Co-authored-by: Sisyphus <clio-agent@sisyphuslabs.ai>
(cherry picked from commit 983a54f76a88f648c393ad5a3ab98968cc2b2ad7)
(cherry picked from commit c740503739dd2c485c83d6bb90e1a0f77aa3b776)
---
 .../src/com/oplus/view/OplusEdrUtils.java     | 41 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/oplus-fwk/src/com/oplus/view/OplusEdrUtils.java b/oplus-fwk/src/com/oplus/view/OplusEdrUtils.java
index 728e4e8f..8b32bbb6 100644
--- a/oplus-fwk/src/com/oplus/view/OplusEdrUtils.java
+++ b/oplus-fwk/src/com/oplus/view/OplusEdrUtils.java
@@ -7,8 +7,11 @@ import android.util.Size;
 import android.view.SurfaceControl;
 import android.view.SurfaceView;
 import android.view.View;
+import android.view.ViewRootImpl;
 
-/* Stub implementation - OxygenOS SurfaceControl EDR extensions not available */
+/* Compatibility shim. The OxygenOS SurfaceControl EDR extensions are not available, so
+ * only the members with a 1:1 AOSP primitive are backed; the rest stay non-throwing
+ * stubs because no artifact maps OplusCamera's dex references to individual methods. */
 public final class OplusEdrUtils {
     public static final int DOLBY_OFF_WITHOUT_ANIMATION = 131073;
     public static final int DOLBY_OFF_WITH_ANIMATION = 131072;
@@ -46,11 +49,26 @@ public final class OplusEdrUtils {
     }
 
     public static SurfaceControl getSurfaceControl(View view) {
-        return null;
+        if (view == null) {
+            return null;
+        }
+        try {
+            ViewRootImpl viewRoot = view.getViewRootImpl();
+            return viewRoot == null ? null : viewRoot.getSurfaceControl();
+        } catch (Throwable t) {
+            return null;
+        }
     }
 
     public static SurfaceControl getBlastSurfaceControl(SurfaceView view) {
-        return null;
+        if (view == null) {
+            return null;
+        }
+        try {
+            return view.getRenderingSurfaceControl();
+        } catch (Throwable t) {
+            return null;
+        }
     }
 
     public static int getLocalHdrVersion() {
@@ -107,6 +125,21 @@ public final class OplusEdrUtils {
     }
 
     public static boolean setEdrSdrRatio(SurfaceControl sc, SurfaceControl.Transaction transaction, float edrSdrRatio) {
-        return false;
+        if (sc == null || transaction == null || !sc.isValid()) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        /* setDesiredHdrHeadroom throws IllegalArgumentException unless the ratio is
+         * finite and either 0 (system chooses) or >= 1.0f. Reject out-of-domain values
+         * rather than clamping: clamping would silently alter what the caller asked
+         * for, while returning false is the "not applied" answer this API already has. */
+        if (!Float.isFinite(edrSdrRatio) || (edrSdrRatio != 0.0f && edrSdrRatio < 1.0f)) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        try {
+            transaction.setDesiredHdrHeadroom(sc, edrSdrRatio);
+            return true;
+        } catch (Throwable t) {
+            return false;
+        }
     }
 }
